# tools/palette_paint_witness.rish -- a palette of color swatches SEEN on a real image proves itself on metal (Season G).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) -- the discrete sibling of image/gradient_paint.rish: where the gradient paints a
# CONTINUOUS ramp, this rung paints a row (or column) of solid color SWATCHES, the palette legend a design surface shows
# beside a picker, a color scale, or a gradient. Stands on the open geometry floor (image/shape.rye fill_rect), the open
# color algebra (image/color.rye), and the open QOI codec (image/qoi.rye).
# Design read: active-designing/20260816-210735_season-g-color-algebra-crux.md (the color floor this stands on).
# Teacher, thanked clean-room: gratitude/w3c-css-color.md (the W3C CSS Color spec + sRGB -- public standards only).
#
# The crux this witness proves is that a palette becomes a real image: paint_palette_h tiles the width with n solid
# swatches, swatch i filling the columns [i*w/n, (i+1)*w/n). Each cell is its color exactly byte-for-byte, the cells are
# contiguous and disjoint (no gap, no overlap, a hard edge at each boundary), an uneven width still tiles exactly, a
# translucent swatch blends src-over, the palette round-trips through the open QOI codec byte-for-byte, the vertical twin
# stacks the swatches, and an empty palette, a zero dimension, a strip too narrow for its swatches, an out-of-bounds box,
# and a too-short vertical strip refuse by name having painted nothing. Compose not braid -- shape owns the fill, qoi owns
# the target, color composites; this rung only routes each swatch to its cell. No network, no key, no funds.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/palette_paint_witness.rish

say "palette-paint: Language EN -- Season G's palette of color swatches painted onto an image; a keeper names a list of colors and reads back a tiled swatch strip a surface can show, on our own color model and open codec."
say "palette-paint: Style Radiant -- compose not braid; shape.fill_rect OWNS the fill, qoi owns the RGBA target, color composites src-over, and this rung only ROUTES each swatch to its cell so a translucent swatch tints the picture beneath."
say "palette-paint: Lens TAME -- the whole rectangle bound-checked ONCE up front in u64 so a far edge can never wrap; the palette validated ONCE before any pixel so a malformed list refuses having painted nothing; the cell partition in u32 so it never wraps; integer boundaries so a strip is deterministic; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/palette_paint"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/palette_paint.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "palette-paint: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "palette-paint: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "palette-paint: ${out}"

assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-palette-paint" else "palette-paint: selftest did not print the GREEN palette-paint line"

assert selftest.out contains "round-trips through the open QOI codec byte-for-byte" else "palette-paint: the painted palette did not prove its QOI round trip"

assert selftest.out contains "tiles the whole width" else "palette-paint: the palette did not prove it tiles the whole strip"

assert selftest.out contains "partitions to widths 2,3,3 tiling exactly" else "palette-paint: the uneven partition did not prove it tiles exactly"

say "palette-paint: GREEN -- a palette of color swatches painted onto a real image (horizontal and vertical), the cells tiling exactly, each swatch its color, its blend true, its round trip byte-for-byte, proven on metal."
